+<a id="unsigned-linux-community-packages"></a>
+
+## Unsigned Linux community packages
+
+On a Linux x64 host, run `pnpm run package:desktop:linux:x64:unsigned` to create an AppImage and a Debian package under `apps/desktop/.desktop-build/targets/linux-x64/unsigned-artifacts/`. Use `pnpm run package:desktop:linux:x64:dir` for the unpacked `linux-unpacked` application. Both commands use the local unsigned application ID, ignore inherited release and signing settings, run the prepared-runtime and assembled-application smoke checks, and write no update release record. Linux packaging rejects signed mode and cannot be published by the official Desktop upload command.
+
+The AppImage and DEB are community distribution formats, not qualified official releases. Distributors must test launch, desktop integration, sandbox behavior, plugin installation, terminal access, native dependencies and upgrade removal on every supported distribution. The packaged executable is `deepseek-harness`; the DEB installs its desktop entry through electron-builder.
+
